@startuml Submission and Evaluation Flow

title Code Submission and Evaluation Flow

actor Student
participant "Submission Service" as SB
participant "Evaluation Service" as EV
participant "Content Service" as CS
participant "Notification Service" as NT
participant "RabbitMQ" as RMQ
participant "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "Redis" as Redis
participant "Piston API" as PS

== Submission Phase ==
Student -> SB: POST /api/v1/submissions\n{assignmentId, code (base64), language}

SB -> DB: INSERT submission\n(status=PENDING)
DB --> SB: submission saved

SB -> RMQ: Publish SubmissionCreatedEvent
SB --> Student: 201 Created + SubmissionResponse

== Evaluation Phase ==
RMQ -> EV: Consume SubmissionCreatedEvent

EV -> CS: GET /assignments/{assignmentId}
CS --> EV: Assignment details with test cases

EV -> EV: Validate language support

alt Language not supported
    EV -> RMQ: Publish SubmissionEvaluatedEvent\n(status=FAILED, result=FAILED, error)
else Language supported
    par For each test case
        EV -> PS: POST /api/v2/execute\n{code, input, language}
        PS --> EV: {stdout, stderr, exitCode}
        EV -> EV: Compare output
    end

    EV -> EV: Calculate overall score and result

    EV -> RMQ: Publish SubmissionEvaluatedEvent\n{status=EVALUATED, result, score, testCaseResults}
end

RMQ -> SB: Consume SubmissionEvaluatedEvent
SB -> DB: UPDATE submission\n(status=EVALUATED, result, score)
SB -> Redis: Evict cache

RMQ -> NT: Consume SubmissionEvaluatedEvent
NT -> Student: Send email/push notification

Note over Student: Poll or refresh to see results
@enduml
